# GNOME desktop — installed on top of the base (system/config/packages.list)
# by scripts/setup-desktop.sh (system stage 5). Comments and blank lines are
# ignored.

# ── GNOME (Wayland) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
gnome-shell
gdm
gnome-session
gnome-settings-daemon
gnome-keyring
gnome-control-center
gnome-themes-extra
adwaita-icon-theme
nautilus
gnome-terminal
# NOT evolution-data-server: only gnome-shell-calendar-server (events in the
# top bar's calendar) links it, and it pulls in a second WebKit
# (webkit2gtk-4.1, ~140M) for its online-account logins. The calendar itself
# works without it; Arch's GNOME leaves it optional too.
# gvfs includes the FUSE daemon on Arch; the backends are split out.
gvfs
gvfs-smb
gvfs-mtp
gvfs-gphoto2
gvfs-afc
gvfs-nfs
gvfs-dnssd
gvfs-wsdd
# No image viewer / PDF viewer / text editor in the core image — the core
# desktop is Nautilus + GNOME Terminal only. Users get Loupe, Papers, Text
# Editor etc. from Flathub.

# ── Portal ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
xdg-desktop-portal-gnome
